  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Zervokhori</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A fortified settlement, probably constructed in the Hellenistic period, located south of the modern Greek village of Asfaka (Souli municipality, Epirus). An extensive, elite residence was built inside the fortification in early Roman times. The modern chapel of Ag. Donatos, which incorporates spolia from a Hellenistic structure, was built on part of the lower terrace of the ancient site.",
